==Greek==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|el|grc|πατήρ}}, from {{inh|el|grk-pro}}, from {{inh|el|ine-pro|*ph₂tḗr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[paˈte̞ras]|lang=el}}

===Noun===
{{el-noun|m|πατέρες|f=μητέρα}}

# [[father]]; a [[male]] [[parent]]
# Father {{gloss|form of address for [[monk]] or [[priest]]}}
# {{label|el|figuratively}} [[founder]] of a [[science]]
# {{label|el|plural}} [[ancestor]]s

====Declension====
{{el-nM-ας-ες-2a|πατέρ}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|priest}} {{l|el|πατήρ|g=m}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|el|μητέρα|g=f|gloss=mother}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|el|πατερούλης|g=m|gloss=diminutive for of father}}
* {{l|el|πατρικός|gloss=fatherly}}
* {{l|el|πατροκτονία|gloss=patricide}}

